---
description: Keep interface, domain, and infrastructure code in separate modules
alwaysApply: false
---

# Separation of concerns

- A module that renders or parses input does not also open a database, a network client, or a file of secrets.
- Domain rules accept already validated values. Validation sits at the boundary that receives the input.
- Infrastructure adapters (clients, queues, the filesystem) hide the vendor API behind a function the domain can call.
- Do not import a host framework into a module whose job is shared behaviour.
- Application-specific rules stay in the application. Do not push them into a shared module to avoid a local edit.

```ts
function assertReady(release: { indexHtml: string }): void {
  if (release.indexHtml.length === 0) throw new Error("Release has no index.");
}
```
